# Copy to .env.local for local development, and set the same values in your
# Vercel project settings for production.

# Required: one model key. Read only by the serverless functions in /api —
# never sent to the browser.
#
# Perplexity is the default. Its Sonar models answer from a live web search and
# cite what they used. Get a key at https://console.perplexity.ai
PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=pplx-...

# Or Claude instead — dearer and doesn't search by default, but it's the one
# that supports MCP connectors and writes replies long enough for the Code
# workspace to build a real page. https://console.anthropic.com → API Keys.
# Set both and Perplexity wins, so the cheaper one is never a surprise.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Optional: accounts, saved chats, and server-side connector tokens.
# Leave these unset and Selflight runs signed-out, storing everything in the
# browser. See supabase/README.md for the ten-minute setup.
#
# The VITE_ prefix is load-bearing: Vite compiles those two into the JavaScript
# it ships to browsers, and refuses to ship anything else. That is what keeps
# the service-role key on the server.

# Project Settings → API → Project URL
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# Project Settings → API → anon public key. Safe in a browser: every table it
# can reach is guarded by row-level security keyed to the signed-in user.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Project Settings → API → service_role secret key. Bypasses all row-level
# security. Server only — never add a VITE_ prefix to this one.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Per user, per calendar month, input and output tokens together. 0 removes it.
#
# 2,000,000 is roughly 430 messages — about 14 a day, which a tester will not
# reach by using the product normally. It's a circuit breaker for a runaway
# script or a shared login, not a budget: the budget is how many people you
# invite. A user who somehow spent all of it costs about $11 on sonar-pro.
# The arithmetic, and how to watch what's actually being spent, is in
# supabase/README.md → Spending.
SELFLIGHT_MONTHLY_TOKEN_CAP=2000000
